    {
      "tile_id": "tile_sql_fund_filtering_rows",
      "title": "Filtering Rows with WHERE and Logical Operators",
      "summary": "Learn to filter query results with WHERE, combine conditions using AND, OR, and NOT, control evaluation order with parentheses, and test for missing values with IS NULL.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "step_id": "tile_sql_fund_filtering_rows.s01",
          "type": "explainer",
          "concept_ids": [
            "sql.where_filtering"
          ],
          "title": "Filtering rows with WHERE",
          "eyebrow": "WHERE clause",
          "lede": "Ask a question of your data by keeping only the rows where a condition is true.",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "prose",
              "block_id": "tile_sql_fund_filtering_rows.s01.p1",
              "text": "SELECT * FROM orders returns every order in the QuickCart database. To answer a real question — which orders took longer than 40 minutes to deliver? — you need to narrow the result to just the matching rows. WHERE takes a search condition and evaluates it for every row. A row is kept only if the condition is true; rows where it is false are discarded.",
              "role": "intro",
              "lineage": {
                "concept_ids": [
                  "sql.where_filtering"
                ],
                "fact_ids": [
                  "sql.where_filtering#f1"
                ],
                "teaching_block_ids": [
                  "sql.where_filtering#tb1",
                  "sql.where_filtering#tb2"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "prose",
              "block_id": "tile_sql_fund_filtering_rows.s01.p2",
              "text": "The comparison operators <, >, <=, >=, =, and <> compare two values of the same or a compatible type and produce a boolean result. = tests for equal; <> tests for not equal (!= is an alias for <>). WHERE customer_id = 2 keeps only orders from customer 2; WHERE delivery_time_minutes <> 20 keeps orders whose delivery time is not 20 minutes.",
              "role": "syntax",
              "lineage": {
                "concept_ids": [
                  "sql.where_filtering"
                ],
                "fact_ids": [
                  "sql.where_filtering#f2"
                ],
                "teaching_block_ids": [
                  "sql.where_filtering#tb3"
                ]
              }
            },
